// MP+rlx -- MP (MP.lit) over relaxed accesses.
//
// Source: Arlt & Vafeiadis, "RGSep under Release/Acquire Consistency",
//         PACMPL 10 (OOPSLA2), Article 375, 2026. doi:10.1145/3839507, Section 3: the MP assertion "does not hold under the relaxed fragment
// of the C++ memory model".
//
// Reference verdicts:
//   the paper: the relaxed fragment of C11 allows reading y = 1 and x != 7.
//   herd7 7.58 on herd/MP+rlx.litmus, under the zoo's abstract-sc, abstract-tso,
//     ra, sra, wra and abstract-coherence cat models and herd's rc11.cat:
//     SC and TSO forbid; RA, SRA, WRA, Coherence and RC11 allow.
// The paper's registers are renamed r -> ry, b -> rb:
// MoRDor reads only names beginning with r as registers.
x := 0; y := 0;
{ x.store(7, rlx); y.store(1, rlx) }
||| { ry := y.load(rlx); rb := x.load(rlx) }
%%
allow (ry = 1 && rb != 7) [RA, SRA, WRA, Coherence, RC11]
forbid (ry = 1 && rb != 7) [SC, TSO]
